# Domain Repositories

## Repository Interface + InMemory Implementation

Repository interfaces and their InMemory implementations live together in `domain/repositories/`. This keeps the domain self-contained and testable.

```java
// src/main/java/com/example/orders/domain/repositories/OrderRepository.java

import java.util.*;

// Interface
public interface OrderRepository {
    void save(Order order);
    Optional<Order> findById(Id id);
    List<Order> findByCustomer(Id customerId);
}

// InMemory implementation (same file)
class InMemoryOrderRepository implements OrderRepository {

    private final Map<String, Order> orders = new HashMap<>();

    public InMemoryOrderRepository(List<Order> initialOrders) {
        if (initialOrders != null) {
            initialOrders.forEach(order ->
                    orders.put(order.getId().getValue(), order)
            );
        }
    }

    public InMemoryOrderRepository() {
        this(List.of());
    }

    @Override
    public void save(Order order) {
        orders.put(order.getId().getValue(), order);
    }

    @Override
    public Optional<Order> findById(Id id) {
        return Optional.ofNullable(orders.get(id.getValue()));
    }

    @Override
    public List<Order> findByCustomer(Id customerId) {
        return orders.values().stream()
                .filter(order -> order.getCustomerId().equals(customerId))
                .toList();
    }
}
```

## Repository Characteristics

- **Domain language**: Use domain terms, not database terms
- **Entity-centric**: Work with domain entities, not primitives or DTOs
- **No implementation details**: The interface doesn't reveal storage mechanism

```typescript
// ⚠️ WORSE - Database-oriented interface
interface OrderRepository {
    void insert(OrderDocument order);
    Optional<OrderDocument> findOne(String id);
}

// ✅ BETTER - Domain-oriented interface
interface OrderRepository {
    void save(Order order);
    Optional<Order> findById(Id id);
}
```

---

## InMemory Repository Characteristics

- **Same interface**: Implements the same contract as the real adapter
- **In-memory storage**: Uses Map, Array, or simple data structures
- **Seed data**: Constructor accepts initial data for test setup
- **Lives in domain**: Part of the domain, not infrastructure

---

## Real Adapter (Infrastructure)

Real adapters implement the repository interface with actual database logic. They live in `infrastructure/adapters/`.

```java
// src/main/java/com/example/orders/infrastructure/adapters/MongoOrderRepository.java
import java.util.*;

public class MongoOrderRepository implements OrderRepository {

    private final MongoCollection<OrderDocument> collection;

    public MongoOrderRepository(MongoCollection<OrderDocument> collection) {
        this.collection = collection;
    }

    @Override
    public void save(Order order) {
        OrderDocument document = toDocument(order);

        collection.updateOne(
                Filters.eq("_id", document.id),
                Updates.combine(
                        Updates.set("customerId", document.customerId),
                        Updates.set("items", document.items),
                        Updates.set("status", document.status)
                ),
                new UpdateOptions().upsert(true)
        );
    }

    @Override
    public Optional<Order> findById(Id id) {
        OrderDocument document = collection.find(Filters.eq("_id", id.getValue())).first();
        return document != null ? Optional.of(toDomain(document)) : Optional.empty();
    }

    @Override
    public List<Order> findByCustomer(Id customerId) {
        List<Order> result = new ArrayList<>();

        for (OrderDocument doc : collection.find(Filters.eq("customerId", customerId.getValue()))) {
            result.add(toDomain(doc));
        }

        return result;
    }

    private OrderDocument toDocument(Order order) {
        Map<String, Object> primitives = order.toPrimitives();

        OrderDocument doc = new OrderDocument();
        doc.id = (String) primitives.get("id");
        doc.customerId = (String) primitives.get("customerId");
        doc.items = (List<?>) primitives.get("items");
        doc.status = (String) primitives.get("status");

        return doc;
    }

    private Order toDomain(OrderDocument document) {
        // Map MongoDB document to domain entity
        return null;
    }
}
```

